 "title": "Veteran Services - Madison County Courthouse Nebraska",
 "text": "Veteran Services - Madison County Courthouse Nebraska\nSkip to content.\nMadison County Courthouse south entrance will be closed beginning at 7:00 A.M. on Wednesday, October 21, 2026, and will remain closed until 12:00 P.M. on Thursday, October 22, 2026.\nX\nMenu\n-->\nEmployment\nCalendar\nAbout\nContact Us\nSearch for:\nMenu\nHome\nDepartments Assessor\nClerk\nCounty Attorney\nCounty Court\nDistrict Court\nElections\nHighway Department\nPublic Defender\nPlanning and Zoning\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nVeteran Services\nNoxious Weed Authority\nCounty Services Budget\nAgendas\nMeetings\nPublic Notice\nProceedings\nBoard of Commissioners\nWhere do I…? Find Election Info\nRegister to Vote\nRegister/Title A Vehicle\nObtain & Learn About Permits\nAgencies Fair Housing\nUtility Bill Assistance\nEmergency Management\nCaring Senior Resources – Emergency Housing Guide\nSenior Housing Net-Emergency Housing Guide\nVisitors Bureau\nUNL County Extension\nMadison County Fair\nMedicare Options for Nebraska Residents\nMedicare Resources for Immigrant Populations\nMedicare Resources for Immigrant Populations-Spanish\nEmployment\nCalendar\nAbout\nContact Us\nVeteran Services\nThe Madison County Veterans Service Office is established under Nebraska Revised Statute 80-407. Under this statute the Madison County Veteran Service Office provides assistance and guidance to Veterans, Widows of Veterans and their families for Federal, State, and County veterans programs and benefits based on the required elements for eligibility.\nFederal Department of Veterans Affairs benefits include Education Benefits, Vocational Rehabilitation, Service-connected disability, Non-service connected disability pension, Health care and burial benefits.\nNebraska Department of Veteran Affairs Programs include Waiver of Tuition, Admission to the Nebraska Veterans Home and Emergency financial assistance through the Nebraska Veterans Aid Fund.\nThe Madison County Veterans Service Office also serves as a trusted and respect partner in collaboration with other community agencies and Veterans organizations as needed to assist Veterans of the Madison County community.\nCome Visit Us in Norfolk\nHelpful Links\nMilitary License Plates\nVeterans Designation on Nebraska License or ID\nNorfolk Veterans Home\nNebraska Department of Veteran Affairs\nNebraska Veterans Aid\nNebraska Affairs Regional Office in Lincoln, NE\nVeteran Affairs General Benefits Information\nOmaha Veterans Affairs Medical Center\nNorfolk Veteran Affairs Community Based Outpatient Clinic\nVeterans Homeless/Near Homeless Assistance\nGregg Hanson\nPhone:\n(402) 370-3578\nFax:\n(402) 370-3579\nEmail:\nSend Email\nLocation:\n1305 S 13 th St\nSuite 200\nNorfolk, NE 68701\nHours:\nMonday-Friday\n8:00 am – 12:00 pm\n1:00 pm – 5:00 pm\nScroll To Top\nAddress\nMadison County Courthouse\n1313 North Main Street\nPO Box 290\nMadison, Nebraska 68748\nPhone: (402) 454-3311\nHours: Mon - Fri 8:00AM - 5:00PM\nHours may vary per office.\nTreasurer's Office 8:30 AM - 5:00 PM\nQuick Links:\nFAQ\nContacts\nEmployment\n©2026 Madison County Courthouse",
